required_SPL_dependency_limits:
  - "Native strong Simple dispatcher must be generated and linked from authenticated_syscall_context_v1; weak/default linkage does not qualify entry."
  - "Actual canonical paging and page-table owner must prepare child roots, own physical frames and supply checked copy/anonymous retirement; this native commit does not admit those SPL changes."
  - "Actual ARM32 hw_shims CP15/TLB/barrier/IRQ exports need generated provider and caller ABI proof; source instruction assembly alone is insufficient."
  - "Common iso Scheduler/IPC owners, authenticated syscall dispatch, checked-copy loan, inherited FD/OFD roles and observer invalidation must all remain in the real execution closure."
  - "Owned loader/spawn caller must transfer actual owners and gate capture delivery with intact architecture qualification; the current legacy caller is not an authenticated tool runner."
  - "Mapped-stack metadata issuer/reader and policy resolver are source-only, import SCC uncompiled; no mapping, native entry, capture or authority follows from their plain data."
  - "SPL ownership has exactly one pending verification batch requiring a proper producer; this native evidence neither consumes nor replaces it."
excluded_from_this_commit_group:
  - "All ARM32 SPL paging/copy/context/anonymous/hardware-provider and metadata changes."
  - "ARM32 diagnostic user C fixture and its README; an object compile is not guest execution."
  - "All shared FD, policy, scheduler, authority registry, observation and compiler changes owned by other lanes."
